From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:27:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-ams968hh01: start the link clock after the
 panel reset

The ANA38401 DDI ignores its init sequence and every read when the DSI
clock lane is in HS while its reset is released, so the panel stayed
dark unless msm.defer_hs_clk=1 was on the command line. Ask the host for
that order with MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_DEFERRED_HS: lanes in LP-11 through the
reset, then the continuous HS clock from the first command on. That is
the vendor order for this panel (qcom,mdss-dsi-lp11-init and
qcom,mdss-dsi-force-clock-lane-hs in dsi_panel_ANA38401_AMS968HH01_
qxga_octa_cmd.dtsi, Samsung's GPL-2.0 kernel source for the SM-T820).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams968hh01.c   | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams968hh01.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams968hh01.c
index 6caf3260e3..75ac95cb4d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams968hh01.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-ams968hh01.c
@@ -712,7 +712,7 @@ static void ams968hh01_gamma_tables(struct ams968hh01 *ctx, const u8 *mtp)
  * The panel's own gamma offsets (MTP): 33 bytes in register 0x83 order,
  * read the vendor way (B0 <offset>, then a generic read of D8) from
  * offset 0x5a. The DDI only answers reads before the init sequence when
- * the link clock starts after the panel reset (msm.defer_hs_clk=1);
+ * the link clock starts after the panel reset (MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_DEFERRED_HS);
  * without the offsets the tables stay those of a panel with zero offsets.
  */
 static int ams968hh01_read_mtp(struct ams968hh01 *ctx)
@@ -856,8 +856,9 @@ static int ams968hh01_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 	msleep(10);
 
 	/*
-	 * The DSI lanes are already in LP11 here (prepare_prev_first). The
-	 * DDI wants 70 ms plus margin between LP11 and reset.
+	 * The DSI lanes are already in LP11 here (prepare_prev_first), the
+	 * clock lane too (MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_DEFERRED_HS). The DDI wants 70 ms
+	 * plus margin between LP11 and reset.
 	 */
 	msleep(75);
 	before = gpiod_get_value_cansleep(ctx->tcon_ready_gpio);
@@ -1068,8 +1069,15 @@ static int ams968hh01_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ctx->dsi); i++) {
 		ctx->dsi[i]->lanes = 4;
 		ctx->dsi[i]->format = MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB888;
-		/* command mode, init commands in LP, continuous clock */
-		ctx->dsi[i]->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
+		/*
+		 * Command mode, init commands in LP. The DDI ignores
+		 * everything when the HS clock runs through its reset, and
+		 * it wants a continuous clock: LP-11 on all lanes through
+		 * the reset, then HS, as the vendor driver does
+		 * (qcom,mdss-dsi-lp11-init, qcom,mdss-dsi-force-clock-lane-hs).
+		 */
+		ctx->dsi[i]->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM |
+					  MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_DEFERRED_HS;
 
 		ret = mipi_dsi_attach(ctx->dsi[i]);
 		if (ret < 0) {
